# T4.2 case 1: the password in the config is wrong.
#
# One connection, so tab 1 is whichever backend the runner points this at.
# What has to hold: the tab ends on ✗, the driver's complaint is in the
# Results pane under the host and port it was talking to, and the retry the
# pane offers is the `c` that is on the keyboard. The runner greps the frames
# for the password itself.
key c
wait busy
expect ✗
expect localhost:
expect cannot connect
expect c to retry
frame wrong-password

# Nothing is connecting any more, so nothing may be drawn: two seconds of
# turns, of which the runner counts the frames traced in the last one.
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
frame wrong-password-idle
key q
